# BASIS CHOICE. Everything here is 6-31G*, not the 6-311+G** of the QM/MM site
# energies. A mixed-basis attempt (opt at 6-311+G**, Hessian at 6-31G*) FAILED:
# TeraChem refused the Hessian with "maximum component of gradient is too large"
# because a geometry stationary in one basis is not stationary in another
# (Grad-Max 2.20e-4 at 6-311+G** vs 6.45e-3 at 6-31G*). A Hessian requires a
# stationary point IN ITS OWN BASIS, so the whole chain must share one.
# 6-31G* is chosen for speed; omega and the Huang-Rhys factor S are far less
# basis sensitive than excitation energies. This must be stated wherever the
# resulting S and omega are used.
# Stage 1: finish the ground-state optimisation on GPU.
# Same functional/basis as the QM/MM site energies (camb3lyp/6-311+gss), so the
# vibronic parameters are consistent with the rest of the pipeline rather than
# coming from a second code at a smaller basis.
# GAS PHASE: pointcharges are deliberately absent. Optimising inside field.pc
# collapses nuclei onto bare MM charges (H42 reached 0.09 A from a -0.568 e
# charge in the first ORCA attempt) -- that file is single-point only.
coordinates geom.xyz
run minimize
new_minimizer yes
method camb3lyp
basis 6-31gs
charge -1
spinmult 1
scrdir scr_opt
scf diis+a
threall 1.0e-13
convthre 1.0e-6
# SPEED: gradient criteria kept at default -- they define the stationary point
# the Hessian needs. Displacement/energy criteria loosened 10x: the residual
# motion is a soft torsion taking 0.05-radius steps, and chasing it to 1.2e-3
# displacement adds cycles without improving the stiff modes we actually use.
min_converge_gmax 4.5e-4
min_converge_grms 3.0e-4
min_converge_dmax 1.8e-2
min_converge_drms 1.2e-2
min_converge_e 1.0e-5
gpus 1
end
